wsrv itself contains no third-party source code: SHA-1, Base64, UTF-8 validation and the
WebSocket and HTTP logic are written in this repository (ADR-0005).

It is built against, and at run time links dynamically to, these system libraries, which are
not distributed with it and keep their own licenses:
  - zlib (zlib License), for permessage-deflate (ADR-0020)
  - OpenSSL 3 (Apache-2.0), for TLS (ADR-0019)
  - the C++ standard library and the C library of your toolchain

Used only to build and test, never shipped:
  - GoogleTest 1.15.2 (BSD-3-Clause), fetched by CMake (cmake/WsrvTests.cmake)
  - Autobahn|Testsuite (Apache-2.0), run from its own container image (tests/autobahn)
  - clang-format, clang-tidy, ccache, and the sanitizers of GCC and Clang

The prebuilt libwsrv.so and wsrvd of a release are dynamically linked to the libraries above
(ADR-0026); the SHA256SUMS file and build attestation of each release identify the files.
